# Line endings: normalise on commit, check out LF everywhere.
#
# The generator writes LF explicitly (newline="\n" in cli.py). Git for Windows
# ships with core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which would check the
# committed data back out as CRLF -- so `uv run generator` would immediately
# rewrite all seven JSON files and `git diff data/` would report changes on
# every single run. That destroys the property the whole eval system rests on:
# a clean clone regenerates byte-identical data.
#
# Fixed here rather than via `git config core.autocrlf false` because this file
# travels with the clone. CI, a second laptop and any future contributor all
# get identical bytes; a machine-level setting is invisible to all of them.
# Same argument as committing uv.lock.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite3 binary
